# cursor-helper: release and changelog (`cursor-helper-release`)

Use when cutting a **cursor-helper** release or updating **`[Unreleased]`** in [`CHANGELOG.md`](../../CHANGELOG.md). This rule applies **only to this repository** — not to consumer projects that symlink `y-rules/`.

**Single source of truth:** [`VERSION`](../../VERSION) (one line, e.g. `1.2.0`).

---

## SemVer policy

| Bump | When |
|------|------|
| **MAJOR** | Removed or renamed commands/rules consumers invoke; symlink install layout change; behavior that breaks existing workflows |
| **MINOR** | New command or rule; new workflow capability; non-breaking enhancements |
| **PATCH** | Wording/clarification only; typo fixes; internal cross-references with no user-visible behavior change |

---

## Changelog writing

Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/). Sections: `Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Removed`, `Deprecated` — include only non-empty sections.

**Audience:** teammates who symlink this repo. Write **what they gain or must do** — not commit SHAs, file paths, or implementation detail.

| Conventional Commit | Changelog section |
|---------------------|-------------------|
| `feat` | Added (or Changed if behavior shifts) |
| `fix` | Fixed |
| `feat!` / `BREAKING CHANGE` | Changed and/or Removed + **MAJOR** bump |
| `docs` (user-visible README/catalog) | Changed |
| `chore` / internal refactors | Usually omit unless users must act |

During normal work, add short bullets under **`## [Unreleased]`** when shipping notable user-visible changes. Not every typo needs a bullet.

---

## When to release

Cut a version when meaningful changes have landed on `main` — not after every commit. Before release, confirm **`[Unreleased]`** lists everything user-visible since the last tag (`git tag -l 'v*'`).

---

## AskQuestion gates (mandatory)

| Step | When | Options (minimum) |
|------|------|-------------------|
| **Version bump** | Before editing `VERSION` | Approve proposed MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH / Edit bump / Cancel |
| **Changelog review** | After drafting the new version section | Approve / Edit changelog / Cancel |
| **Commit** | Before `git commit` | Commit now / Edit / Cancel |
| **Tag** | Before `git tag` | Create tag / Skip tag / Cancel |
| **Push** | Before `git push` or tag push | Push branch and tags / Push branch only / Done — no push |

**Hard rule:** Do **not** commit, tag, or push until the matching gate is answered.

---

## Release steps

1. Read [`VERSION`](../../VERSION) and [`CHANGELOG.md`](../../CHANGELOG.md); gather bullets from `[Unreleased]` and recent `git log` if needed.
2. **`AskQuestion`** — confirm version bump (MAJOR / MINOR / PATCH).
3. Move `[Unreleased]` content to `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` (today's date).
4. Leave an empty `## [Unreleased]` section at the top.
5. Update [`VERSION`](../../VERSION) to match.
6. **`AskQuestion`** — changelog review.
7. Stage `CHANGELOG.md` and `VERSION` (and README version line if it changed).
8. Commit: `chore(release): vX.Y.Z`
9. **`AskQuestion`** — tag gate. If approved: `git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "vX.Y.Z"`
10. **`AskQuestion`** — push gate.

---

## Git history safety

- **Do not** rebase, amend past commits, or rewrite history as part of a release.
- Retroactive tags on old SHAs are annotations only — they do not change commit hashes or dates.
- Tag `vX.Y.Z` points at the **release commit** that bumps `VERSION` and finalizes the changelog section.

